// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`prompt builders (snapshots) > explain prompt 1`] = `
"Model: v8 detect, scale n, input 640, 80 classes.
Goal: Detect small road damage (cracks and potholes) in dashcam video frames. Must run on a Raspberry Pi 5 (CPU only). The dataset has 3 classes.
Number of classes: 3
Classes: longitudinal crack, transverse crack, pothole
Typical object size: 10–40 px wide in a 640 px frame (thin cracks)
Image resolution: 1920×1080 dashcam frames, resized to 640
Class imbalance: potholes are rare compared with cracks
Dataset notes: shadows, tar patches and road markings look similar to cracks
Deployment target: Raspberry Pi 5 (4-core ARM CPU, no GPU), ONNX Runtime
Budget / latency constraint: keep the model small; aim for a few frames per second on the Pi
Reading level: eli5.
Explain these nodes (return one entry per node id, same ids):
- n9: layer 9 SPPF [1024,5] in backbone, output 256×20×20 P5/32; builtin; receives from n8 (C2f, 256×20×20); sends to n10 (Upsample); n20 (Concat).
- n15: layer 15 C2f [256] in neck, output 64×80×80 P3/8; builtin; receives from n14 (Concat, 192×80×80); sends to n16 (Conv); n22 (Detect head).
- n22: layer 22 Detect head ["nc"] in head, output 64×8400 ; builtin; receives from n15 (C2f, 64×80×80); n18 (C2f, 128×40×40); n21 (C2f, 256×20×20); sends to the predictions."
`;

